## Terminology

Use **Checklist** in all user-facing copy, REST paths (`/checklists`), table names (`launchdek_checklists`), PHP classes (`LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_*`), and JS (`initChecklists`, `data-launchdek-page="checklists"`). Legacy `workflow_*` identifiers exist only in DB migration and backward-compat audit/webhook reads — never in new code.

## Architecture

- Bootstrap defines constants, requires all classes, registers activation/deactivation hooks, calls `launchdek_run_plugin()`.
- `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin::run()` wires admin UI, `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API::register()`, `LAUNCHDEK_Drift_Cron::register()`.
- `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin::init()` on `init`: `LAUNCHDEK_Installer::maybe_install()`, `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::register()`, `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::seed_builtin()`, `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::sync_builtin()`.
- Settings: `launchdek_settings` via `LAUNCHDEK_Settings` (group `launchdek_settings_group`). Global kill switch: `enabled`. `exclude_options` blocks sensitive `/wp/v2/settings` fields from API checklist payloads on remote sites (`LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::filter_excluded_payload()`). `client_panel_layout` (default `sidebar`) controls how the optional client checklist panel renders on remote wp-admin; `client_panel_title` (default `Agency Checklist`, max 80 chars) sets the panel heading — both pushed in run snapshots via `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push::build_snapshot()`.
- Custom tables via `LAUNCHDEK_Installer` (`DB_VERSION` `1.4.0`, option `launchdek_db_version`). All DB access through `*_Repository` classes. Upgrades from pre-1.1.0 rename `launchdek_workflows` → `launchdek_checklists`, `workflow_id` → `checklist_id`, and migrate legacy capability keys via `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::migrate_workflow_caps()`. Upgrades to 1.2.0 add `launchdek_sites.client_agent` and `launchdek_runs.client_run_token`. Upgrades to 1.3.0 add `launchdek_run_steps.notes_json` for per-step client evidence. Upgrades to 1.4.0 add `launchdek_runs.is_archived` (soft-hide from site history; archive via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::archive()`, permanent delete via `::delete()`).
- Remote calls: `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client` (Application Password basic auth) — never store plaintext passwords outside vault. `request()` tries pretty `/wp-json/` first, then `?rest_route=` when the response is `rest_no_route` (broken rewrites on local/MAMP installs).
- Checklist engine: `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Runner::start()` creates run → `execute_next()` / `auto_advance()` / `execute_all_auto()` → `LAUNCHDEK_Step_Executor` → `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper` for `api` steps; `manual` steps set `awaiting_manual` until `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete` (revert via `/uncomplete` → `LAUNCHDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()`). Failures trigger `LAUNCHDEK_Webhook_Dispatcher`. Step admin paths resolve via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` — priority: explicit `deep_link` (`normalize_stored_path()`), API route/payload inference (`path_from_api_step()` for `/wp/v2/settings` and common core REST routes), then title/instructions keyword inference (`infer_path_from_text()`). On checklist save, `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository` stores `deep_link` as a normalized admin path (not `esc_url_raw()`). Hub run tracker and client snapshots use `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::admin_link()` for full URLs; snapshots also include `admin_path` so the client panel can rebuild local `admin_url()` links. `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::repair_builtin_deep_links()` (once via `launchdek_deep_links_repaired`) restores paths stripped by legacy URL sanitization.
- Client checklist panel: `LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed()` deploys the bundled `mu-plugin/` files when a site is saved, connection-tested with credentials, or when `push_run()` is called with `$sync_bundle = true` (initial push and manual **Refresh Client Panel**). `push_run( $run_id, $prepare = true, $sync_bundle = null )` — `$sync_bundle` defaults to `$prepare`; auto-advances API steps when `$prepare` is true; pushes a run snapshot to the remote panel (`POST /launchdek/v1/client/run`); uses `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::ensure_client_token()` for per-run `client_run_token` callbacks (backfills legacy runs). `sync_run()` calls `push_run( $run_id, false, false )` — snapshot-only re-push with no step advancement and no bundle reinstall. Hub run handlers call `sync_run()` after hub-side step advances. Client token callbacks (`/client-runs/...`) pass `$skip_client_sync = true` — hub returns `snapshot` in the response instead of re-pushing; client panel applies it locally (optimistic UI with rollback on error). Client manual completions/uncompletions hit hub `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete|uncomplete` with `X-LaunchDek-Run-Token`. Client notes save locally first on the remote site, then sync to hub; hub snapshots merge notes via `filter_step_notes()` / `merge_step_notes()` rather than wiping local entries. Sites REST responses expose `client_agent` when the panel is detected.
- Admin UI: thin partials in `admin/partials/` with `data-launchdek-page`; JS drives CRUD via REST (`launchdekAdmin` global). Checklists use a vertical drag-and-drop canvas builder with step config sidebar (multicheck role mapping dropdown, live deep-link inference via `POST /checklists/infer-deep-link`, per-step `show_note_field` / `show_screenshot_field` toggles, API payload mapper).
- Dashboard cache: `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache` stores stats, connection health counts, the 15-entry live log feed, and quick-launch picker options (`quick_launch`: lightweight `sites` + `checklists` id/title pairs via `LAUNCHDEK_Site_Repository::picker_list()` / `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::picker_list()`, max 100 each) in `launchdek_dashboard_cache` (non-autoload). Feed entries include `show_site_label` (from `LAUNCHDEK_Audit_Log::feed_entry_show_site_label()`) so site-scoped actions render a separate site badge instead of embedding the site name in the message text. Repositories call `invalidate_stats()` / `invalidate_connections()` / `invalidate_quick_launch_picker()` on site/checklist mutations; `LAUNCHDEK_Audit_Log::log()` calls `invalidate_feed()`. Dashboard PHP partial and `launchdekAdmin.dashboard` localize preloaded stats, connections, feed, and `quickLaunch` on first paint; Quick Launch Bar selects render server-side with `data-launchdek-preloaded="1"` (JS skips REST fetch when preloaded). REST `/dashboard/*` and `/logs/feed` (default) read from cache.
- Activity logs: dedicated hidden submenu page (`PAGE_SLUG . '-activity-logs'`, registered then `remove_submenu_page`) reachable from Sites toolbar, dashboard feed link, and legacy `?page={slug}-sites&activity_logs` redirect. Full filtered audit table via `GET /logs/feed?detailed=1` (`can_view_dashboard`); supports `site_id`, `status`, `date_from`, `date_to`, `search`, `limit` (default 200). Automation page audit panel still uses `/audit` (`can_view_audit`).
- Sites page run history: each site row has a chevron toggle (`.launchdek-site-history-toggle`) that expands a nested runs panel (`.launchdek-site-runs-row` → `.launchdek-site-runs-panel`); loads `GET /sites/{id}/runs` on first expand via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::list_for_site_history()` (lean JOIN + batched step progress; default `limit` 25, optional `offset`, returns `{ runs, has_more, offset, limit }`; cached in JS with in-flight deduplication and **Load more** pagination). Table shows Steps column (fraction + status badge + progress bar). **View run** is a split button with dropdown for Edit (blocked for built-in template runs), Duplicate, Export, Archive (`POST /runs/{id}/archive`), and Delete (`DELETE /runs/{id}` — uses shared confirm modal). Site row Actions use Edit + dropdown (Push Checklist, Test); combined Connection + Health badge in Status column.
- Dashboard onboarding: activation redirect (`?onboarding=1`) opens a 2-step modal — **Step 1**: paste plain-text SOPs with placeholder-as-sample live preview, or **Start from a template** via the shared template picker (`importMode: populate` loads steps into paste/preview); **Step 2**: optional existing-site picker or new-site connect/test (App Passwords) → create checklist + site + first run. Segmented progress UI with labeled step hints. Dismissal persisted via `onboarding_dismissed` (`POST /onboarding/dismiss`, `can_view_dashboard`); Settings can re-show via `POST /onboarding/reset` (`can_manage_settings`) + **Show onboarding wizard** button. Modal markup in `launchdek-onboarding-modal.php` (required on dashboard + settings); logic in `initOnboarding()` (global init, not dashboard-only). Auto-opens only on the dashboard screen when `onboarding.show` is true (not on Settings after save); `?onboarding=1` still opens on any page with the modal. Exposes `window.launchdekOpenOnboarding`.
- Template picker: shared modal (`launchdek-template-picker-modal.php`) with capsule category filters, selectable template list, steps preview panel, **Start blank instead**, and **Import Template**. Included on dashboard, checklists, and settings. Checklists **New Checklist** tab **Start from Template** opens picker → default `importMode: checklist` via `POST /templates/{slug}/clone` → `onImport(checklist)` opens **My Checklists** builder; onboarding uses `importMode: populate` to fill paste text. Logic in `initTemplatePicker()` (global init); exposes `window.launchdekOpenTemplatePicker(callbacks)`.
- Checklists page sections: unified `nav-tab-wrapper` (`.launchdek-checklist-nav`) with four tabs — **Templates** (default — built-in category grid, custom checklists, agency vault), **My Checklists** (dropdown picker `#launchdek-checklist-select`, builder + import/export), **New Checklist** (intro card with **Start from Template** / **Start Blank** / **Browse Templates**), and **Auto-Capture** (inline panel, not a modal). Tab panels use `[data-launchdek-tab-panel]` (`templates|my-checklists|new-checklist|auto-capture`); tab state via `?tab=` (`templates` clears param) or `?checklist_id={id}` (opens **My Checklists**; legacy `?tab=builder` normalizes to `my-checklists`). Template/built-in cards use **Use Checklist** (`createChecklistFromTemplate()` → `openChecklistEditor()`); custom cards show **Edit Checklist** + **Use Checklist** side by side (`duplicateChecklist()` fetches full checklist then clones). Legacy `?page={slug}-templates` redirects to Checklists (`maybe_redirect_legacy_templates_page()`).
- Custom checklist list performance: `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list()` returns lightweight rows (`id`, `title`, `description`, `steps_count`, step id/title preview); `GET /checklists?summary=1` (optional `is_template`, `is_vault`); `GET /templates/vault` uses the same summary shape. Checklists screen preloads non-template summaries in `launchdekAdmin.customChecklists`; admin JS deduplicates via `fetchCustomChecklistSummaries()` / `refreshCustomChecklistUi()` (one request instead of three for grid, picker, and vault select).
- Auto-capture: user-initiated recording on a connected client site with the checklist panel installed. Hub `LAUNCHDEK_Auto_Capture` proxies to remote `GET|POST|DELETE /launchdek/v1/client/capture`; client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Auto_Capture` hooks admin actions (REST settings, plugin toggles) into manual/api steps stored in `launchdek_client_capture` option. Checklists **Auto-Capture** tab panel (`#launchdek-panel-auto-capture`, `.launchdek-auto-capture-panel`) uses hub `/sites/{id}/capture` routes; **Import Captured Steps** loads steps into the builder and switches to **My Checklists**.
- Remote architecture: targets need WP 6.0+ with Application Passwords enabled. Core API checklist steps use only core REST. The optional client admin panel is a lightweight mu-plugin bundle auto-installed from the hub — not a separate plugin download.

## Admin Pages

Use `LAUNCHDEK_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` — never hardcode slug strings.

| Page | Slug | Partial | JS init |
|------|------|---------|---------|
| Dashboard | `PAGE_SLUG` | `launchdek-admin-page.php` | `initDashboard()` |
| Sites | `PAGE_SLUG . '-sites'` | `launchdek-sites-page.php` | `initSites()` |
| Activity Logs | `PAGE_SLUG . '-activity-logs'` | `launchdek-activity-logs-page.php` | `initActivityLogs()` |
| Checklists | `PAGE_SLUG . '-checklists'` | `launchdek-checklists-page.php` | `initChecklists()` + `initTemplates()` |
| Automation & Audit | `PAGE_SLUG . '-automation'` | `launchdek-automation-page.php` | `initAutomation()` |
| Integrations | `PAGE_SLUG . '-integrations'` | `launchdek-integrations-page.php` | `initIntegrations()` |
| Settings | `PAGE_SLUG . '-settings'` | `launchdek-settings-page.php` | `initSettings()` + Settings API form |

Checklists partial has four tab panels (`data-launchdek-tab-panel="templates|my-checklists|new-checklist|auto-capture"`) toggled via `.launchdek-checklist-nav` nav tabs (not page-title actions). Templates panel hosts built-in grid, vault, and custom checklist cards — no separate admin submenu. My Checklists panel uses `#launchdek-checklist-select` dropdown (replaces sidebar list). Activity Logs is a hidden submenu (no sidebar entry) — link from Sites toolbar or dashboard feed.

Menu capability: `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::admin_menu_capability()` (`launchdek_view_dashboard`). Settings page render checks `MANAGE_SETTINGS` even though the submenu uses the menu cap.

## REST Permission Callbacks

`LAUNCHDEK_REST_API` delegates to `can_*()` methods — always add matching callbacks for new routes:

| Callback | Capability |
|----------|------------|
| `can_view_dashboard` | `VIEW_DASHBOARD` |
| `can_manage_sites` | `MANAGE_SITES` |
| `can_edit_checklists` | `EDIT_CHECKLISTS` |
| `can_execute` | `EXECUTE_CHECKLISTS` |
| `can_view_audit` | `VIEW_AUDIT` |
| `can_manage_settings` | `MANAGE_SETTINGS` |

## Custom Capabilities

`LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities` — use `::current_user_can( $cap )` for permission checks (respects `role_permissions` settings). `manage_options` always passes. Settings UI uses `get_agency_role_presets()` (Admin/Developer/Auditor archetypes) and `get_capability_labels()` for the role-permission matrix.

| Constant | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `VIEW_DASHBOARD` | Dashboard + menu access |
| `MANAGE_SITES` | Site CRUD, connection tests |
| `EDIT_CHECKLISTS` | Checklist/template CRUD |
| `EXECUTE_CHECKLISTS` | Run control, drift verify |
| `VIEW_AUDIT` | Audit log access |
| `MANAGE_SETTINGS` | Settings page |

## REST API (`launchdek/v1`)

Registered in `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API`. Auth: `X-WP-Nonce` (`wp_rest`) + capability callbacks.

| Group | Routes |
|-------|--------|
| Dashboard | `/dashboard/stats`, `/connections/ticker`, `/logs/feed` (cached feed; `?detailed=1` bypasses cache for full audit query), `/onboarding/dismiss`, `/onboarding/reset` |
| Sites | `/sites`, `/sites/{id}`, `/sites/{id}/test`, `/sites/test`, `/sites/tags`, `/sites/{id}/runs` (checklist run history for expandable site rows; optional `status`, `limit` default 25 max 200, `offset`; returns `{ runs, has_more, offset, limit }` via `list_for_site_history()`), `/sites/{id}/panel/install` (retry panel bundle deploy), `/sites/{id}/capture` (GET status, POST start/stop, DELETE clear), `/panel/bootstrap` (manual mu-plugin loader download) |
| Checklists | `/checklists` (optional `summary=1` → `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list()`; optional `is_template`, `is_vault`), `/checklists/{id}`, `/checklists/import`, `/checklists/infer-deep-link` (POST — `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` for builder live inference), `/checklists/{id}/export`, `/checklists/{id}/validate-step` |
| Runs | `/runs/batch`, `/runs` (optional `push_to_client` bool, default true), `/runs/{id}` (GET `can_execute`; DELETE `can_manage_sites` — permanent delete), `/runs/{id}/archive` (POST `can_manage_sites` — soft-hide from history), `/runs/{id}/next`, `/runs/{id}/auto`, `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete`, `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete`, `/runs/{id}/push-client` (`push_run( $id, false, true )` — snapshot re-push + bundle sync, no auto-advance), `/client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete`, `/client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete`, `/client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/notes` (token auth via `X-LaunchDek-Run-Token`; `$skip_client_sync`, returns `snapshot`) |
| Audit/Drift | `/audit/meta`, `/audit`, `/drift/status`, `/drift/verify`, `/drift/verify/{id}` |
| Templates | `/templates`, `/templates/vault` (summary rows via `summary_list( is_vault => true )`), `/templates/{slug}/clone` |
| Integrations | `/integrations`, `/integrations/{slug}/push`, `/integrations/telemetry-rules` |

## Database Tables

`{prefix}launchdek_sites` (`client_agent` flag), `launchdek_site_tags`, `launchdek_checklists`, `launchdek_runs` (`client_run_token`, `is_archived`), `launchdek_run_steps` (`notes_json` per-step note array), `launchdek_audit_log`, `launchdek_connection_events`. Bump `LAUNCHDEK_Installer::DB_VERSION` for schema changes.

## Client Checklist Panel (mu-plugin)

Bundled under `mu-plugin/` and deployed to remote `wp-content/mu-plugins/` by `LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer`. Loader: `launchdek-client.php`; classes in `launchdek-client/`:

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| `LAUNCHDEK_Client_REST_API` | Remote routes under `launchdek/v1/client/*` |
| `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store` | Active run snapshot CRUD, `user_can_complete_step()` (all logged-in users when no `target_roles`), local note save/merge, `patch_from_hub_run()`, `panel_title` from snapshot (`get_panel_title()` / `sanitize_panel_title()`) |
| `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Panel` | Admin panel UI + asset enqueue (`wp_enqueue_media()` for optional screenshot attachments; layout from snapshot `panel_layout` — `sidebar` (default), `live_topbar`, `bottom_dock`, `floating_pill`, `toast`, `admin_menu`, `fullscreen`, `focus_mode`, `inline_metabox`; legacy `left_sidebar` / `split_panel` fall back to `sidebar`; body class `launchdek-client-layout-{layout}`; admin bar shortcut for bar/flyout layouts; `inline_metabox` registers post/page editor metabox); panel collapses to tab via **Collapse** — collapsed/minimized chrome (sidebar tab, floating pill, toast, top/bottom bar, fullscreen launcher, admin bar badge, `admin_menu` progress trigger button) shows live progress via `formatCompactProgress()` / `syncAdminBarProgress()` on step toggles; `admin_menu` collapsed shows `.launchdek-client-admin-menu-trigger` (progress button) instead of hiding the root; `inline_metabox` collapse keeps panel chrome with `.launchdek-client-panel-collapsed-meta` (step · percent); steps collapsed by default — title + status; chevron expands actions/notes; per-step note sections toggle individually (prefs in `localStorage`); compact settings deep-link icon (`.launchdek-client-step-settings-link`) when `deep_link` URL present (resolved from snapshot `deep_link` or `admin_path` via `resolve_step_deep_link()`); optional per-step note field via `show_note_field`; screenshot attach button gated by `show_screenshot_field` (requires `show_note_field`); notes require non-empty text, save locally first, optional `attachment_id`/`attachment_url` via media library; completed steps show SVG double-tick icon, `completed_by` name/email and `completed_at`; completed runs stay visible with Started/Completed summary and **Dismiss** button) |
| `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Hub_Client` | Callbacks to hub with run token |
| `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Auto_Capture` | Records admin actions into checklist steps during capture sessions |

Remote client REST routes (authenticated via Application Password or logged-in client user):

| Route | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `GET /client/info` | Panel presence/version probe (public) |
| `POST /client/install` | Receive bundled files from hub (`can_hub_manage`) |
| `GET|POST|DELETE /client/run` | Read/push/clear active run snapshot |
| `POST /client/run/dismiss` | Clear a completed checklist from the client panel (local snapshot only) |
| `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/complete` | Client completes manual step → hub callback |
| `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/uncomplete` | Client reverts completed manual step → hub callback |
| `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/notes` | Client saves note locally first, then syncs to hub (`hub_synced` in response); notes require non-empty text; optional `attachment_id`/`attachment_url` from remote media library |
| `GET|POST|DELETE /client/capture` | Read/start/stop/clear auto-capture session (requires panel) |

Hub-side orchestration: `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push` (`push_run`, `sync_run`, `complete_client_step`, `uncomplete_client_step`, `add_client_step_note`, `build_snapshot` — includes `panel_layout` and `panel_title`). Token callbacks use `$skip_client_sync = true` and return `snapshot` for local client apply — no redundant hub→client re-push on step toggles. Step notes stored on hub as `{ user, text, created_at, attachment_id?, attachment_url? }`; `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::filter_step_notes()` / `::step_notes_match()` dedupe empty/duplicate notes. `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::all()` excludes archived runs by default (`include_archived` opt-in); `::list_for_site_history()` returns paginated lean rows with batched `steps_total` / `steps_completed` / `progress_percent`. Automation run tracker renders notes (author · timestamp) and attachment thumbnails; hub-side **Mark Not Complete** posts `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete`. Sites page **Push Checklist** modal posts `POST /runs` with `push_to_client`. Automation page **Refresh Client Panel** (`#launchdek-run-push-client`) posts `POST /runs/{id}/push-client` (`push_run( $id, false, true )`). Deep-link to a run via `?page={slug}-automation&run_id={id}`. Audit actions: `client_run_pushed`, `client_step_completed`, `client_step_uncompleted`, `client_step_note_added`, `manual_step_uncompleted`, `run_archived`, `run_deleted`.

